fter seven patients had been enrolled. The company has now formally dropped the program, according to its fourth-quarter earnings materials. Bayer is instead prioritizing AB-1009, another AAV gene therapy for late-onset Pompe disease that recently entered a Phase 1/2 U.S. trial and has received FDA Fast Track and Orphan Drug designations. The move reflects a portfolio consolidation strategy in a challenging competitive field, where several Pompe disease programs have faced regulatory setbacks or discontinuation.\n\n## 4.3. Green light\n\n### 4.3.1. Affinia\n\n<visual_element id=\"e2\">\nAffinia Therapeutics logo: Rectangular horizontal logo with a gray background. A turquoise and green geometric arrow-like symbol appears on the left, followed by the word \"affinia™\" in large white lowercase letters. \"THERAPEUTICS\" appears underneath in smaller, widely spaced white capital letters.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUurea tsükli häire – Kliinilised uuringud – Teabe ja Kliiniliste Uuringute Ülevaade (https://kliiniliseduuringud.ee/haigus/uurea-tsukli-haire/uurea-tsukli-haire-kliinilised-uuringud/)\nciteturn195search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Uuringu kestus: Uuring toimub eeldatavasti augustist 2025 kuni juulini 2026. ... „Long-Term Safety Study of HepaStem for Patients with Urea Cycle Disorders, Crigler-Najjar Syndrome, and Fibroinflammatory Liver Diseases”.\n\n## Allikad\n\n  1. clinicaltrials.eu. Vaadatud: 29.07.2026.\n  2. „Long-Term Safety Study of HepaStem for Patients with Urea Cycle Disorders, Crigler-Najjar Syndrome, and Fibroinflammatory Liver Diseases”. European Clinical Trials Information Network. Vaadatud: 23.07.2026.\n\n## Käimasolevad kliinilised uuringud Uurea tsükli häire\n\n  * #### Uuringu eesmärk on hinnata ravimi CMP-CPS-001 ohutust tervetel vabatahtlikel ja patsientidel, kellel on muutunud ornitiin-transkarbamülaasi geen\n\nVärbamine pole alanud\n\n1 1\n\nUuritavad haigused:\n    * U